-   262	13. **Role write boundary (BLD-12), enforced by macOS.** Every role process tree of a Build
-   263	    runs inside one macOS Seatbelt profile, applied by the kernel at launch
-   264	    (`/usr/bin/sandbox-exec -p <profile>`). That covers the fresh Developer, every resume, the
-   265	    Reviewer, their native helpers, hooks (including Stop and any `make` it or the Developer
-   266	    starts), `mix kogen.expert` and the Expert it launches, and anything any of them spawns.
-   267	    Descendants inherit the profile and can't remove it. The mechanism was chosen by probing
-   268	    (`evidence/write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md`). Neither harness's own permission layer
-   269	    confines the harness process's own writes (the Write tool, apply_patch, session files),
-   270	    and Codex's Seatbelt can't nest inside another profile.
-   271	    - **One Build-wide profile.** `Kogen.Build.WriteBoundary` renders it once at admission
-   272	      from canonical, symlink-resolved paths. It is `(allow default)`, then
-   273	      `(deny file-write*)`, then writes allowed only under:
-   274	      - the Candidate;
-   275	      - the Build's harness home;
-   276	      - a spaceless per-Build temp dir under the controller's canonical system temp dir,
-   277	        `kogen-build-<build-id>/`. It is created at admission and removed at every Build exit,
-   278	        and every launch gets it as `TMPDIR`, `TMPPREFIX` (zsh here-documents) and
-   279	        `CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR` (Claude Code's Bash tool);
-   280	      - `KOGEN_RAW_LOG_DIR` when the controller has it set (retained evidence, created by the
-   281	        controller at admission if missing; it must not be or contain the control root,
-   282	        control's `.git`, `.kogen/build.lock` or `.kogen/runtime/scenario-tracking/`);
-   283	      - the stdio and pty devices;
-   284	      - the login keychain file and its `.sb-` temp files, because Claude Code persists
-   285	        rotated OAuth tokens through `/usr/bin/security` in-process;
-   286	      - `<Claude scope>/.oauth_refresh.lock` when the route uses Claude Code;
-   287	      - the Codex scope when the route uses Codex, minus the entries Kogen's scope validation
-   288	        refuses or owns: `hooks.json`, `plugins/`, `rules/`, `config.d/`, `AGENTS.md`,
-   289	        `AGENTS.override.md`, `environments.toml`, `agents/` and `.kogen-owned`.
-   290	
-   291	      `/bin/ps` is the one executable run outside the profile, because sandboxed processes
-   292	      can't exec setuid binaries and Kogen's own code reads the process table with it.
-   293	      LaunchServices opens (`lsopen`) and Apple Events (`appleevent-send`) are denied, because
-   294	      they hand work to processes outside the profile. The same profile applies to every role
-   295	      of the Build, so an Expert on the other harness runs inside the Developer's profile.
-   296	    - **Everything else is refused, and named.** Writes to the control checkout (including
-   297	      `.kogen/`, the build lock and the tracking record), control's Git metadata (the
-   298	      Candidate's index, objects, refs and config live there, so role `git add`, `commit`,
-   299	      `stash`, `checkout -b`, `update-ref` and `config` fail), other Candidates, other harness
-   300	      homes, owner records, the Claude scope directory, the user's home and every other path
-   301	      fail with `EPERM` ("Operation not permitted"). That includes writes through symlinks,
-   302	      hardlinks, renames and `/tmp` aliases. Reads, network and process execution stay open.
-   303	      Role `git status` and `git diff` still work.
-   304	    - **The launcher.** `Kogen.Harness` Build role launches (adapters' `run_with_stdin`, the
-   305	      Codex review and exec paths, Build readiness such as `claude auth status` and
-   306	      `codex login status`) take the boundary from the launch context and prefix the command.
-   307	      Readiness runs inside the boundary too, so a grant a real harness needs fails before any
-   308	      model call. Shape, login, status outside a Build, and Shaping sessions are not wrapped.
-   309	      Their containment is the Shaping half of BLD-12, owned by
-   310	      `headless-shaping-and-question-inbox`. Every wrapped launch sets `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` to
-   311	      the profile sha256. Kogen's own state root (`~/Library/Application Support/Kogen/…`:
-   312	      runtimes, selectors, Codex `operations/` and `active/` leases) is outside the grants. So
-   313	      `mix kogen.expert` run from the Developer's tree in a Build takes no Codex lease and makes
-   314	      no operation dir there. It uses the frozen binding from `KOGEN_EXPERT`, puts its
-   315	      operation root under the harness home, and relies on the lease the Build controller
-   316	      already holds for that harness from admission to exit (`Harness.open_roles/3`).
-   317	    - **Fails closed.** Every grant is resolved to its canonical path first, because the
-   318	      kernel matches only real paths and `/tmp/…` or `/var/folders/…` aliases would silently
-   319	      never match (probe 14). If `/usr/bin/sandbox-exec` is missing, a grant can't be resolved
-   320	      to an existing directory, a grant is `/`, `/private/tmp`, `/private/var`, `$HOME`, the control
-   321	      root or one of its ancestors, or the admission self-test (the profile applied to
-   322	      `/usr/bin/true`) fails, admission stops before any readiness call or launch, naming the
-   323	      reason. There is no unwrapped fallback.
-   324	    - **Already confined.** The kernel refuses to apply a different profile inside a sandbox
-   325	      (`sandbox_apply: Operation not permitted`, probe 2). Confinement is detected by the kernel,
-   326	      never by the environment: applying `(version 1)(allow default)` to `/usr/bin/true` exits 71
-   327	      only inside a sandbox. If the controller is confined and `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` is set (a
-   328	      fixture Build that a Developer runs in its own shell, or `mix kogen.expert` from the
-   329	      Developer's tree), role launches run without re-applying and the record says `inherited`.
-   330	      They are still inside the enclosing role's boundary. If it is confined without the marker,
-   331	      the Build stops naming the foreign sandbox. If it is not confined, the marker is ignored
-   332	      and the profile is applied.
-   333	    - **The controller stays outside.** The parent controller and its own verification children
-   334	      (#4: `make check` and the selected targets, `make -C <Candidate>`) run unconfined, with
-   335	      `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` removed from their environment. The controller must write the
-   336	      record, lock and receipts, and fixture Builds inside `check` and live targets must apply
-   337	      their own boundary, which the kernel would refuse inside another profile.
-   338	    - **Kept flags.** Claude Code keeps `--dangerously-skip-permissions`. Codex keeps
-   339	      `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` and `--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust`. The
-   340	      enforcement is the enclosing kernel profile, which already covers everything those
-   341	      harness layers would, including the harness's own writes, and Codex's own Seatbelt would
-   342	      fail to nest inside it (probe 10). README says so.
-   343	    - **Record.** The tracking record gains a `boundary` block: mode (`applied` or `inherited`),
-   344	      the profile sha256, the grant list, the denied scope entries and the `sandbox-exec` path.
