-   216	## Open for the Shaper (2026-09-24, B1 reshape)
-   217	
-   218	The Draft currently assumes the recommended answer to each question.
-   219	
-   220	### Q1. Where Candidate worktrees live — settled 2026-09-24
-   221	
-   222	Shaper: "inside Kogen's own tree". CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md nesting is
-   223	unimportant because those files are not wanted in projects; duplicate trees
-   224	in the repository are the cost to avoid. The location is
-   225	`~/Library/Application Support/Kogen/build-workspaces/<project-id>/`. Tests
-   226	redirect the root with `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`, like `KOGEN_CLAUDE_ROOT`, so
-   227	automated tests never write to the real Kogen directory; the Shaper asked
-   228	what this meant and was answered.
-   229	
-   230	### Q2. Kept Candidates: stop message and commands — settled 2026-09-24
-   231	
-   232	The Shaper's answers across three rounds:
-   233	
-   234	- A Kogen command for kept Candidates is wanted, not bare git commands.
-   235	- A list command is required: "git worktree list is useless - it doesn't
-   236	  show which worktree belongs to which intent and the worktree names are
-   237	  obfuscated". Names must be readable and list must show the Intent.
-   238	- Publish is dropped: "publish is weird because it's pretty much useless".
-   239	  An accepted Build already fast-forwards automatically.
-   240	- Remove is added. Guard accepted only: deleting a stopped Candidate's
-   241	  uncommitted edits is fine on request, but a Candidate holding an accepted
-   242	  commit not reachable from its admitted branch needs `--discard-accepted`.
-   243	- Prune is added. Removing orphans left by deleted or moved checkouts, the
-   244	  only cross-project action, needs an explicit flag, "because it's an
-   245	  unexpected behavior".
-   246	- Every command acts on the current project only.
-   247	
-   248	Narrowed after independent review (2026-09-24): the Shaper forwarded a
-   249	review recommending cutting `prune` and `--orphans` to make B1 more likely to
-   250	land first time, and said "the agent was right / these other commands are
-   251	unnecessary for now / we can either add those as part of parallel builds or
-   252	even as a separate intent". B1 keeps `mix kogen.candidates` (list) and
-   253	`mix kogen.candidates.remove <build-id> [--discard-accepted]`. Prune, orphan
-   254	cleanup and the `project.json` they needed are parked in
-   255	`.kogen/runtime/shaping-followups/SHAPE_CANDIDATE_PRUNE.md`. They are not
-   256	approved backlog. The command names were not vetoed.
-   257	
-   258	The same review's item 3 was also accepted ("the agent was right"): both
-   259	live fixtures' `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` paths contain a space.
-   260	
-   261	### Q3. The Codex route's hook configuration — settled 2026-09-24
-   262	
-   263	The Shaper chose "Support, document limit": both routes use the same
-   264	control-root hook mechanism. It is documented that native Codex reads hook
-   265	*configuration* (`.codex/hooks.json`) from the Candidate, which is structural
-   266	separation, not hostile containment. Codex routing is proved offline only, and
-   267	no `live-native` target is added.
-   268	
-   269	### Parallel Builds in this Intent? — answered, not reopened
-   270	
-   271	The Shaper asked whether B1 allows parallel Builds and how much work adding
-   272	them would be, noting: "it might be too much ... when one build has merged
-   273	automatically, but then the other one needs to rebase main into it, rerun
-   274	the tests, maybe even fix conflicts". Answer: B1 does not allow them; the
-   275	global lock stays. B2 needs a per-Build lock and state, same-Intent refusal,
-   276	the pinned engine (the 2026-09-23 probe showed a running controller can pick
-   277	up code another Build publishes) and serial publication. Without rebase and
-   278	re-verification (brief 22), the second of two parallel Builds is kept
-   279	unpublished and must be rebuilt, which limits B2's value until integration
-   280	exists. The agreed order A → handoff → B1 → B2 stands unless the Shaper says
-   281	otherwise.
-   282	
-   283	## Carried forward (settled, not reopened)
-   284	
-   285	- All investigation, integration and repair happen in the Build's own worktree. Unverified
-   286	  changes are never installed on `main` to be fixed there.
-   287	- When `main` has not moved, publication needs no artificial merge or duplicate
-   288	  verification. When it has moved, B1 refuses. Bringing newer `main` into a Candidate needs
-   289	  fresh verification and Review and is a later Intent (brief 22).
-   290	- Future continuation uses the existing `mix kogen.build <slug>` command, not a separate
-   291	  resume command (brief 20). This does not settle its eligibility rules.
-   292	- Concurrent Builds, per-Build locks and the pinned engine are B2.
-   293	- The control checkout must be clean at publication; all work happens in worktrees
-   294	  (2026-09-23).
-   295	- No silent fallbacks (2026-09-23).
-   296	
-   297	## Not B1
-   298	
-   299	- Route naming: `decisions.md` (2026-09-23) records the Shaper asking for `claude` and
-   300	  `chatgpt`, but the committed config and README name `claude` and `codex`. That belongs to
-   301	  the named-routes follow-up, not this Intent.
