-## Blocking
-
-- **The stated boundary and the grants contradict each other.** The Shaper’s requirement says roles and helpers cannot write outside their Build’s worktree ([questions.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/questions.md:27)). Outcome 13 grants writes to the harness home, temp directory, raw-log directory, Keychain file, Claude refresh lock, and much of the Codex login scope—all outside it ([INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:262), [INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:271)). The fake receipt is deliberately written under the outside harness home ([scenarios.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/scenarios.yaml:469)). **Minimal fix:** state and approve the exact necessary exceptions, or redesign the homes and credentials to meet the literal worktree-only requirement.
-
-- **The raw-log grant permits writes into another Build’s Candidate.** The proposed rejection checks whether `KOGEN_RAW_LOG_DIR` *contains* control, but does not reject a directory *inside* control or another Candidate ([INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:280), [scenarios.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/scenarios.yaml:544)). The live Shape fixture defaults its log directory to the installing checkout’s `.kogen/runtime/live-evidence` and passes a child of it to the nested Build ([live_shape_to_build_test.exs](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/test/kogen/live_shape_to_build_test.exs:294), [live_shape_to_build_test.exs](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/test/kogen/live_shape_to_build_test.exs:561)). **Minimal fix:** never grant an arbitrary inherited raw-log path to roles. Put role-generated logs and probe receipts in that Build’s harness home, then have the unconfined controller retain them.
-
-- **`inherited` does not enforce the nested Build’s boundary.** A nested Build launched in a role shell inherits the *outer* Candidate, harness-home and temp grants; the package acknowledges these are not its own grants ([INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:324), [risks.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/risks.yaml:172)). The marker proves no profile identity and is set in a role-controlled environment. A confined nested Build can therefore write outside its own worktree while reporting `inherited`. **Minimal fix:** refuse nested Builds as an enforced isolation mode; keep inheritance only for the Expert within its already admitted Build, or add an enforceable nested identity and grant check.
-
-- **The named paid proof can pass with a real Codex Reviewer outside the profile.** Offline tests use fake Codex launches; `live-reviewer-rework` checks successful verdicts, a self-reported `applied` record and absence of newly created denied names, but specifies no attempted outside write from the real Codex process tree ([scenarios.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/scenarios.yaml:611), [scenarios.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/scenarios.yaml:621)). An implementation that wraps fake Codex but launches managed Codex unwrapped could pass those checks. The real Expert is likewise exercised only as a fake ([scenarios.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/scenarios.yaml:623)). **Minimal fix:** add a fixture-controlled outside-write attempt from the managed Codex Reviewer’s actual process tree and assert `EPERM`; test the Expert launch through that same production path.
-
-- **The all-fixtures promise needs a migration inventory.** Outcome 13 wraps every fake role, while existing fakes invoke Stop scripts and write state in `.kogen/runtime/` ([INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:534), [fake_codex](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/test/support/fake_codex:7), [fake_hybrid](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/test/support/fake_hybrid:23)). The package names only the outside `stage` write and Shaping case, although its own lesson records 47 failed tests from the earlier confinement attempt ([INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:537), [risks.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/risks.yaml:115)). Probe 9 did **not** establish a passing full gate: both runs failed five tests ([write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md:66)). **Minimal fix:** require an audit of every fake role and hook’s write destinations, with each outside write moved to the trusted test process or a Build-owned grant.
