-## Advisory
-
-- **The mechanism does not establish a general no-escape claim.** The evidence proves one `launchctl bootstrap` and `submit` attempt failed, and demonstrates that `open` succeeded until `lsopen` was denied ([write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md:74)). An allow-default profile leaves other IPC and service delegation unassessed; the cited probes also test *creating* a hardlink across the boundary, not writing through a pre-existing hardlink in a granted tree ([write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md:58)). **Minimal fix:** narrow the physical-impossibility claim to tested local file operations, or add hostile pre-existing-link and service-delegation controls before claiming it for every route.
-
-- **`live-reviewer-rework` is justified under D8, but its assertion is too weak.** It is the existing target that runs a managed Codex Reviewer through a hybrid Build; the default Shape target runs Claude roles ([questions.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/questions.md:196), [verification_targets.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/priv/kogen/verification_targets.yaml:75)). Its need is real because the Codex scope writes are provider behavior ([write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md:67)). Strengthen this target as above. No additional paid target is required by the named scenarios.
-
-- **The broader Codex scope and Keychain grants are security exceptions, not incidental plumbing.** The profile permits role writes to `auth.json`, `config.toml`, rollouts and the login Keychain file ([INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:284), [scenarios.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/scenarios.yaml:598)). They are supported by the observed Keychain and Codex behavior ([write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md:67), [write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/write-boundary-probe-2026-09-25.md:69)). **Minimal fix:** describe them explicitly as writable shared login state and keep the denied Codex entries and native settings validation.
-
-- **No missing guard or unexplained selector found.** The write-boundary source, tests, support, README and workflow paths are covered by `may_change_guarded_paths` ([intent.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/intent.yaml:224)); the missing file selectors are expressly assigned for Developer creation, and the `rehearse-*` names are catalog rehearsal IDs ([INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:500), [verification_targets.yaml](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/priv/kogen/verification_targets.yaml:82)). The boundary module, env marker, record block and test tag each have stated callers or proofs; the raw-log grant is the avoidable extra capability.
-
-- **D9’s controller constraints are correctly identified, but remain a build gate.** Main byte-checks the PreToolUse registration at each Developer launch, passes Claude settings by path, and enables project settings; edits there would affect the installing Build itself ([verification_policy.ex](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/lib/kogen/verification_policy.ex:59), [claude.ex](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/lib/kogen/harness/claude.ex:153), [INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:346)). The fixture-only `.claude/settings.json` plan avoids loading its probe into those roles ([INTENT.md](/private/tmp/claude-501/kogen-prep5b/kogen/.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/INTENT.md:378)). Keep the catalog, hooks, Stop scripts, settings, prompts, Makefile and config byte-identical during installation; the assumed #4 controller must also keep verification children outside role process trees.
