roller verification, the report, the review packet and Jev, an exact-session resume, and each fresh Reviewer.","wrong_result":"Roles run in the Candidate but the report says \"no changes\", or a missing selector looks present, because Git and file checks still read control; the Codex Reviewer trusts control and ignores the Candidate's project files; or a fallback `File.cwd!()` hides a missing root."},{"evidence":"A controller test with a fixture whose control passes and Candidate fails asserts the failed receipt, the Candidate id and the resumed session, and repeats it with tampered Candidate hook copies. A byte-comparison test asserts the three hook and settings paths are unchanged from the admission commit and that the PreToolUse registration matches.","given":"A Build whose Candidate `make check` fails while control's passes, and whose Candidate copies of `.codex/hooks/check.sh`, `stop_runner.py` and `verification_policy.py` are edited to always pass or allow.","id":"controller-judges-candidate","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/build.ex","lib/kogen/build/**","lib/kogen/verification_policy.ex","test/kogen/candidate_verification_test.exs","test/kogen/verification_policy_test.exs","test/kogen/verification_ownership_lifecycle_test.exs","test/support/**"],"offline":["test/kogen/candidate_verification_test.exs","test/kogen/verification_policy_test.exs","test/kogen/verification_ownership_lifecycle_test.exs"],"paid_reason":"offline-sufficient: the controller runs real Make targets in a fixture with a passing control and a failing, hook-tampered Candidate; the verdict path has no provider semantics","paid_target":"none"},"then":"The parent controller runs `make check` and each selected target with cwd equal to the Candidate, records a failed receipt bound to the Candidate id, and resumes the same Developer session through the normal retry path. The tampered hook copies change no receipt or verdict. `VerificationPolicy.preflight` checks the Candidate's hook files. Aft