arget":"live-shape-to-build"},"then":"The Developer, both resumes and both Reviewers run with cwd equal to the same single Candidate and use the same harness home. No second worktree or harness home is created. The resumed session is the same session id. Allowance counting, Jev handling and Review freshness are unchanged. In the real fixture Build, the Claude Code Developer resumes its session in the Candidate after a controller-failed verification, the real Reviewer runs in that Candidate, the fixture's main is fast-forwarded to the Intent commit, and no Candidate worktree or branch remains.","when":"The controller resumes the exact Developer session for the failed verification, resumes it again for the Review finding, and a fresh Reviewer reviews the reworked Candidate.","wrong_result":"Each outer attempt creates a new worktree and loses the Developer's edits; resume runs in another cwd or config dir where Claude Code cannot find the session; or the Reviewer reads control instead of the Candidate."},{"evidence":"Offline publication tests assert the commit parent is A, control status after the fast-forward, removal of the Approved copy, worktree, branch and owner record, the kept harness home, the untracked-file refusal, and fault injection before the fast-forward.","given":"An accepted Candidate while control is clean, attached to B, and B is still at A.","id":"publication-unmoved-main","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/build.ex","lib/kogen/build/workspace.ex","lib/kogen/build/evidence.ex","lib/kogen/git.ex","test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs","test/kogen/commit_provenance_test.exs","test/kogen/commit_failure_rollback_test.exs"],"offline":["test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs","test/kogen/commit_provenance_test.exs","test/kogen/commit_failure_rollback_test.exs"],"paid_reason":"offline-sufficient: real git fixtures for commit, fast-forward, synchronization and cleanup; the real publication is also observed by same-candidate-rework's live run","paid_target":"none"},"then":"One commit with the Intent title, source changes and Complete package is created in the Candidate under today's size limits, `.kogen/runtime/` rejection, index-flag refusal, trailers and commit hooks. B is fast-forwarded to it with control's index and working tree synchronized, and control's HEAD, tree and clean status are asserted. Control's ignored Approved copy of this slug is removed. The Candidate worktree is removed without `--force`, the branch with `git branch -d`, and the owner record is deleted; the harness home is kept. `git worktree list` is back to its pre-Build entries. `build-summary.json` and `evidence.md` resolve the full record from control. No merge commit, rebase or re-verification happens. If the Candidate holds an untracked file, removal is refused, the Candidate is retained and reported, and B is still published.","when":"The controller publishes.","wrong_result":"It commits in control from Candidate bytes; updates the ref with `update-ref` and leaves control's index stale; force-removes a Candidate holding untracked files; leaves the branch behind; or deletes the harness home before the transcripts can be audited."},{"evidence":"Offline tests cover each refusal cause and fault injection between the checks and the fast-forward, asserting refs, control bytes, the retained Candidate and the exact message fields.","given":"An accepted Candidate while B has moved, control is dirty, or control is on another branch.","id":"publication-refused","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/build.ex","lib/kogen/build/workspace.ex","lib/kogen/git.ex","test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs","test/kogen/commit_failure_rollback_test.exs"],"offline":["test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs","test/kogen/commit_failure_rollback_test.exs"],"paid_reason":"offline-sufficient: real git fixtures for moved-branch, dirty-control and other-branch refusals with retained-Candidate and message assertions","paid_target":"none"},"then":"B, control's index, working tree 