e Approved package stays in control. The new Build creates a new Candidate and harness home and never adopts, reuses or deletes a retained one or any foreign worktree.","when":"Each Build stops, and afterwards a new Build of the same Intent is started.","wrong_result":"A stop deletes the Candidate and loses the evidence; the message omits it; or the next Build reuses the old worktree or harness home and inherits its edits or sessions."},{"evidence":"A fake-harness Build whose fake Developer, mid-turn, triggers the control-side writes asserts acceptance and publication, the untouched other packages, and two negative controls: an own-package mutation in the Candidate and a tracked edit in control.","given":"A running Build of slug S, and a control checkout in which, while the Developer's turn is in progress, another session writes a new Draft under `.kogen/intents/drafts/`, edits another Draft, moves another package into `.kogen/intents/approved/`, and runs a fake Shape session against the same login scope.","id":"shaping-during-build","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/build.ex","lib/kogen/build/guarded_paths.ex","lib/kogen/build/workspace.ex","test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs","test/kogen/approved_mutation_test.exs","test/kogen/guarded_paths_test.exs","test/support/**"],"offline":["test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs","test/kogen/approved_mutation_test.exs","test/kogen/guarded_paths_test.exs"],"paid_reason":"offline-sufficient: guard capture, changed paths and publication are controller code over a real git fixture; no provider semantics","paid_target":"none"},"then":"The Build is accepted and published: none of those control writes appears in changed paths, guarded-path capture, the Candidate id or the report, and control is clean for publication. The other packages are untouched by publication, and only S's Approved copy is removed from control. An edit to S's own Approved copy inside the Candidate still fails the Build as an approved mutation. A tracked-file edit in control during the Build makes publication refuse with the Candidate retained.","when":"The Build verifies, is reviewed and publishes.","wrong_result":"Guard capture or changed paths still read control, so the mid-Build Draft fails the Build as in Build l5Ur5WAvyOJvG1lpq92XjGv_; publication removes or moves another package; or the Build's own Approved copy becomes editable."},{"evidence":"Offline command tests with two real Git projects, a live-lock control and path and owner-record mismatch controls assert exact outputs and the surviving and removed paths, refs, homes and records.","given":"Two control checkouts of different projects share one spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`. Project P has a stopped Candidate with uncommitted edits, an accepted-unpublished Candidate, a `running` Candidate whose Build holds the lock, and a stale `running` record whose Build is gone. Project Q has a stopped Candidate. P also has a foreign worktree.","id":"candidate-commands","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/build/workspace.ex","lib/mix/tasks/kogen.candidates.ex","lib/mix/tasks/kogen.candidates.remove.ex","test/kogen/candidates_command_test.exs","README.md"],"offline":["test/kogen/candidates_command_test.exs"],"paid_reason":"offline-sufficient: real two-project git fixtures with running-lock, accepted-unpublished, foreign-worktree and owner-record mismatch controls","paid_target":"none"},"then":"List shows only P's Candidates with build id, slug, title, status (the stale one as `stopped: interrupted`), start time, branch and path. Remove deletes a stopped Candidate's worktree, branch, harness home and owner record; refuses the running one; refuses the accepted-unpublished one without `--discard-accepted` and deletes it once its commit is reachable from the admitted branch; refuses an id that is not P's, and a path that does not match its owner record or is not registered in P's `git worktree list`. Q's Candidate, the running Candidate and the foreign worktree survive. Ea