-.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:11781:     "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs runs the fake Codex role against a disposable scope-shaped directory and asserts each denied entry, the allowed writes and the retained flags. harness_role_test.exs runs `mix kogen.expert` inside a real outer profile against a fake managed Codex runtime under a disposable `KOGEN_CODEX_ROOT` (the managed open path, since `KOGEN_HARNESS` skips leases), and asserts that the Expert launch succeeds and the `active/` and `operations/` entries there are unchanged; codex_environment_test.exs asserts the Build temp `TMPDIR` and flags on Codex launches. The paid live-reviewer-rework run asserts, in `test/support/live_reviewer_rework_fixture.ex`, the retained nested record's boundary block, one SessionStart receipt per Codex Reviewer session id (from the retained raw-log copy) with the refused outside attempts, the absent escape file and ref, and the denied names against a pre-Build snapshot of the scope's top-level entries. Probe 20 showed real Codex 0.156.1 runs a project SessionStart hook on `exec` and `exec resume` inside the profile.",
