f slug S, and a control checkout in which, while the Developer's turn is in progress, another session writes a new Draft under `.kogen/intents/drafts/`, edits another Draft, moves another package into `.kogen/intents/approved/`, and runs a fake Shape session against the same login scope.","id":"shaping-during-build","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/build.ex","lib/kogen/build/guarded_paths.ex","lib/kogen/build/workspace.ex","test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs","test/kogen/approved_mutation_test.exs","test/kogen/guarded_paths_test.exs","test/support/**","priv/kogen/test-reliability.yaml","priv/kogen/test-reliability-remediation.yaml"],"offline":["test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs","test/kogen/approved_mutation_test.exs","test/kogen/guarded_paths_test.exs"],"paid_reason":"offline-sufficient: guard capture, changed paths and publication are controller code over a real git fixture; no provider semantics","paid_target":"none"},"then":"The Build is accepted and published: none of those control writes appears in changed paths, guarded-path capture, the Candidate id or the report, and control is clean for publication. The other packages are untouched by publication, and only S's Approved copy is removed from control. An edit to S's own Approved copy inside the Candidate still fails the Build as an approved mutation. A tracked-file edit in control during the Build makes publication refuse with the Candidate retained.","when":"The Build verifies, is reviewed and publishes.","wrong_result":"Guard capture or changed paths still read control, so the mid-Build Draft fails the Build as in Build l5Ur5WAvyOJvG1lpq92XjGv_; publication removes or moves another package; or the Build's own Approved copy becomes editable."},{"evidence":"Offline command tests with two real Git projects, a live-lock control and path and owner-record mismatch controls assert exact outputs and the surviving and removed paths, refs, homes and records.","given":"Two control checkouts of different projects share one spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`. Project P has a stopped Candidate with uncommitted edits, an accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit is not reachable from its admitted branch, a second accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit the Shaper has since fast-forwarded onto that branch, a `running` Candidate whose Build holds the lock, and a stale `running` record whose Build is gone. Project Q has a stopped Candidate. P also has a foreign worktree.","id":"candidate-commands","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/build/workspace.ex","lib/mix/tasks/kogen.candidates.ex","lib/mix/tasks/kogen.candidates.remove.ex","test/kogen/candidates_command_test.exs","README.md","priv/kogen/test-reliability.yaml","priv/kogen/test-reliability-remediation.yaml"],"offline":["test/kogen/candidates_command_test.exs"],"paid_reason":"offline-sufficient: real two-project git fixtures with running-lock, accepted-unpublished, foreign-worktree and owner-record mismatch controls","paid_target":"none"},"then":"List shows only P's Candidates with build id, slug, title, status (the stale one as `stopped: interrupted`), start time, branch and path. Remove deletes a stopped Candidate's worktree, branch, harness home and owner record; refuses the running one. For a Candidate holding a commit, the matrix is exact: commit reachable from the admitted branch (for example after the Shaper fast-forwarded it, or `published: cleanup refused`) is removed without a flag; commit not reachable is refused without `--discard-accepted` and removed with it. Remove refuses an id that is not P's, and a path that does not match its owner record or is not registered in P's `git worktree list`. Q's Candidate, the running Candidate and the foreign worktree survive. Each command prints what it removed or refused.","when":"From P the Shaper runs `mix kogen.candidates` and `mix kogen.candidates.remove <id>`, with and without `--discard-accepted`.","wrong_result":"List shows every project's worktrees or unnamed git paths; or remove deletes another project's Candidate, a foreign worktree, a running Candidate or an accepted commit without the flag."}]}}
