d-or-exhausted-state\"}`; repair succeeds with dispatch; receipt accepted; `action_count: 4`.\n  - flawed: corrupted state dispatches (`failures:1`), exhausted state still dispatches then returns failure 4, receipt rejected for missing timestamp; `action_count: 6`.\n- `evidence/current-prerequisite-receipt.json` records the complete run exit 0 and hashes:\n  - `stateful_guardrail.py`: `ac09f276...f92d0a`\n  - control: `810f8448...2b263`\n  - mode: `37a40f08...b9ec1`\n- Ownership/limits: `evidence/facts.json:3-5` says fixture sources are read-only and Shaping may write only its Draft; controls establish fixture behavior, not provider access, full-route correctness, or later application correctness. `fixture-contract.md` explicitly says source/action marker must remain unchanged.\n\nConsequential uncertainties: “malformed” validation is narrow—complete mode checks only dict-ness, presence, and numeric comparison of `failures`; malformed types (e.g. non-comparable/string values) can raise runtime errors rather than return the guardrail rejection. The fixture does not establish persistence/concurrency/crash semantics, real provider behavior, or integration with the application route.","started_at":1789998802,"completed_at":1789998861,"duration_ms":59085,"time_to_first_token_ms":6996}}
